---
source: tests/help_pages.rs
description: "a command's -h and --help pages as this build renders them at 100 columns without color; any change to an about, a flag, a value, a heading or the layout changes them: review with cargo insta review, or re-accept with INSTA_UPDATE=always cargo test --test integration help_pages:: and review git diff tests/snapshots/"
---
==> omaddons robot-docs -h <==
Print documentation for agents

Usage: omaddons robot-docs [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  guide          Print the agent guide as Markdown
  schema         Print the JSON Schemas, or one command's
  errors         Print every error and warning code
  install-skill  Install the agent guide as a coding agent's skill

Examples:
  omaddons robot-docs                        the agent guide, as Markdown
  omaddons robot-docs schema install --json  one command's data schema
  omaddons robot-docs install-skill          the guide as a Claude Code skill

Global: -t <TARGET>  --json  --dry-run  -v  --quiet  --no-color  --offline  (--help lists them all)
==> omaddons robot-docs --help <==
Print documentation for agents

The agent guide (bare robot-docs), the JSON Schemas and the error catalog.

Usage: omaddons robot-docs [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  guide          Print the agent guide as Markdown
  schema         Print the JSON Schemas, or one command's
  errors         Print every error and warning code
  install-skill  Install the agent guide as a coding agent's skill

Examples:
  omaddons robot-docs                           the agent guide (the same as robot-docs guide)
  omaddons robot-docs schema --json             every schema: envelope, events, commands, files
  omaddons robot-docs schema install --json     the data of one command
  omaddons robot-docs schema backup restore     a nested command, by its path
  omaddons robot-docs errors --json             every error and warning code

See also: capabilities, help

Global options:
      --json             One JSON envelope on stdout
      --format <FORMAT>  Output format [possible values: json, human]
  -t, --target <TARGET>  The client to act on: id, game mode, family, path, or all [alias: --flavor]
      --dry-run          Show the plan without changing anything
      --actor <ACTOR>    Who is acting: human, agent or widget [env: OMADDONS_ACTOR]
      --reason <TEXT>    Why, recorded verbatim in history
      --offline          Fail any network access [env: OMADDONS_OFFLINE=1]
      --while-running    Allow folder changes while the client runs (never SavedVariables)
      --no-color         No ANSI color
      --no-progress      No progress output
      --progress <MODE>  Progress events on stderr [possible values: json, human, none]
      --quiet            Only errors on stderr
  -v, --verbose...       More detail (repeatable)
  -h, --help             Show help

Learn more: omaddons robot-docs guide
